{"ticker":"FMCC","generated_at_utc":"2026-10-22T00:31:52.060553Z","profile":{"name":"Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corporation","exchange":"OTC Markets OTCQB","country":"United States","sector":"Financial Services","industry":"Mortgage Finance","website":"https://www.freddiemac.com","summary":"Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corporation operates in the secondary mortgage market in the United States. The company operates through two segments: Single-Family and Multifamily. The Single-Family segment purchases, securitizes, and guarantees single-family loans; and manages single-family mortgage credit and market risk, as well as manages mortgage-related investments portfolio, single-family securitization activities, and treasury functions. This segment also serves mortgage banking companies, commercial banks, regional banks, community banks, credit unions, HFAs, savings institutions, and non-depository institutions. The Multifamily segment engages in the purchase, securitization, and guarantee of multifamily loans; issuance of multifamily K certificates; manages multifamily mortgage credit and market risk; and invests in multifamily loans and mortgage-related securities. It also serves banks and other depository institutions, insurance companies, money managers, central banks, pension funds, state and local governments, REITs, non-depository institutions, and brokers and dealers. Federal Home Loan Mortgage Corporation was incorporated in 1970 and is headquartered in McLean, Virginia."},"stats":{"price":3.42,"marketCap":2223203840.0,"revenueGrowth":0.339,"operatingMargins":0.6948,"fcfMargin":null,"netCash":-3288990040064.0,"trailingPE":null,"priceToSales":0.090374134,"beta":1.736,"debtToEquity":43.96694,"fiftyTwoWeekLow":2.7,"fiftyTwoWeekHigh":11.94,"avgVolume":2300909.0},"bars":[{"d":"2025-10-22","o":11.76,"h":11.94,"l":10.99,"c":11.03,"v":2493800},{"d":"2025-10-23","o":11.12,"h":11.42,"l":11.09,"c":11.36,"v":1101700},{"d":"2025-10-24","o":11.35,"h":11.35,"l":10.51,"c":10.63,"v